        "titulo": "The crucial distinction: place (instrumental) vs. movement (accusative)",
        "explicacao": "The crucial distinction: place (instrumental) vs. movement (accusative). Here is a trap that catches almost every learner. The prepositions ПОД and ЗА change case according to the meaning: Place (rest) = instrumental. Movement = accusative. Look. The rule: place (where it is) = instrumental; movement (where it goes) = accusative. English hides this because \"under the table\" is the same whether the cat is lying there or running there. It is the same logic you already saw with В and НА in lesson 16 (where = prepositional; where to = accusative). Here: where = instrumental; where to = accusative. Two prepositions in this group never change: НАД (above) and ПЕ́РЕД (in front of) always take the instrumental, and МЕ́ЖДУ (between) normally does too. So the trap is really about ПОД and ЗА. Compare with В and НА (lesson 16). Notice: the accusative is always the case of movement. The case of rest changes: prepositional with В/НА, instrumental with ПОД/ЗА.",
