        "titulo": "Endings and master table of the instrumental",
        "explicacao": "The instrumental method. Now the endings. The method is the same as always: STEP 1: find the nominative form (the dictionary form). STEP 2: add the instrumental ending, which depends on the gender. STEP 3: done, the noun is in the instrumental. Notice: masculine and neuter get -ОМ/-ЕМ. Feminine in -а/-я gets -ОЙ/-ЕЙ (or the older, poetic -ОЮ/-ЕЮ). Feminine in -ь gets -ЬЮ. Neuter in -мя gets -ЕНЕМ. The big difference from the other cases: masculine and neuter both get -ОМ/-ЕМ (not -У, not -Е). It is a single ending. Then comes the master table of the instrumental. Watch the spelling rule: after the letters ж, ч, ш, щ, ц, an unstressed -ОМ/-ОЙ is written -ЕМ/-ЕЙ: това́рищ → това́рищем (not \"това́рищом\"); врач → врачо́м (stressed, so it stays -ом); муж → му́жем (not \"мужом\"); ноша → но́шей.",
