        "titulo": "The preposition с/со and the pronouns in the instrumental",
        "explicacao": "The С / СО variation. The preposition с (with) has a spelling variant. С is used before most words: с дру́гом, с ма́мой, с учи́телем. СО is used before words that begin with a hard-to-say cluster of consonants (for example с, ш, ж or в followed by another consonant) and before мн-, and it is also used in the very common со мной (with me): со мной, со стака́ном, со всеми́. Why? Ease of pronunciation again. «С дру́гом» is easy to say. But stacking several consonants in a row (с + мн, с + вс) would be a mouthful, so Russian inserts an -о- as a cushion: со мной. English does something similar with \"a\" and \"an\". The personal pronouns in the instrumental. As in the dative, the personal pronouns have special instrumental forms, and you have to learn them. Watch the rule of the \"н\": when он, она́, оно́, они́ come after a preposition, they get an н- at the start: с ним (with him), с ней (with her), с ни́ми (with them), о нём (about him: prepositional), к нему́ (to him: dative). But when the pronoun does not follow a preposition, there is no н: его́ (his / him, with no preposition), её (her), их (their / them).",
